# Patch 0080 — Kavacha AI sidebar: page summarization + natural-language
# history search (ROADMAP Phase 6; ADR 0014). Two roadmap items in one patch
# because they are one surface: "summarize this" and "where did I read about
# this" are the same question asked of the same two engines — patch 0078's
# personal index for retrieval, patch 0079's bridge for generation — and
# splitting them would have produced two half-sidebars.
#
# WHY A SIDEBAR AND NOT THE 0079 PANEL. Patch 0079 printed its summary into an
# arrow panel. A summary is read WHILE browsing: the panel dismissed on the
# first click into the page it had just summarized, could not be resized, and
# had nowhere to put the source list ask-your-history needs. Firefox's classic
# sidebar is already alive in Kavacha (measured: sidebar-box opens at 216px in
# the horizontal-tab layout) and its <browser> is non-remote, so a chrome page
# there has the privileges to call the engines directly. The 0079 panel stays —
# it is the right surface for the tab assistant's one-sentence reports.
#
# REGISTRATION IS AT RUNTIME, NOT IN FIREFOX'S FILE. Firefox declares sidebars
# in a literal Map in browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js, a file Zen
# already patches. KavachaAISidebar calls registerPrefSidebar() — the same
# entry point Firefox uses for its own pref-gated sidebars — once per window
# from ZenStartup, so Kavacha adds a sidebar without editing an upstream file
# and without joining the rebase queue on that Map. Gated on
# kavacha.ai.enabled: switch AI off and the entry disappears.
#
# WHY NATURAL-LANGUAGE SEARCH NEEDED A NEW MODULE. The index matches with LIKE
# and ANDs every term (no FTS5 in mozStorage — ADR 0012). Ask it "where did I
# read about flood mapping in Kerala?" and it looks for one page containing
# "where" AND "did" AND "read" AND … and returns nothing, always. So
# KavachaAskHistory is a retrieval layer, not a prompt: strip the question to
# content terms, try AND, RELAX to OR when that is thin (ranking by how many
# distinct terms a page carries), add Places title/URL hits for pages whose
# text was never captured, then hand the model numbered passages and require
# [n] citations. Measured on the built browser: the question above reduces to
# flood / mapping / kerala and finds the paper.
#
# DEGRADATION IS A FEATURE, NOT AN ERROR PATH. No model, model off, model
# unreachable, or sources with no captured text all return the ranked source
# list with a plain sentence saying why — the question simply becomes a
# search. Retrieval never needed the model; only the prose did.
#
# SAFETY. Model output is untrusted text rendered by a CHROME document, so it
# only ever reaches the screen through KavachaMarkdown (patch 0052), which
# builds DOM nodes and never parses HTML, or through textContent. Citations
# are linkified by walking text nodes and replacing them with elements this
# code created. An innerHTML here would be script execution as chrome.
#
# ALSO FIXED HERE: patch 0079 pointed "Summarize This Page" at
# zen-icons/selectable/edit.svg, which is not in the icon set — the same defect
# class the 0051-0058 audit found eleven of. All 30 Kavacha command icons were
# fetched against the built browser afterwards; none 404.
#
# Summarize no longer depends on the index being ON: the indexer actor gained
# an on-demand Capture query that returns the page text WITHOUT storing it.
# Summarizing what you are looking at should not require having stored it.
#
